    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0324" n="306" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p1/pg306"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790B.00/10–1751: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in India </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-20T15:19:00-05:00">October 20,
                            1951—3:19 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>853. Embtel 1378 Oct. 17. FYI Dept believes highly unlikely KMT troops wld submit
                    to being repatriated by any means. Question our position therefore largely
                    academic.</p>
                <p>You shld not raise question but if asked you may say that US Govt wld give
                    sympathetic consideration to any proposal that Thakin Nu or Nehru might make for
                    repatriation thru Burm. FYI Dept however opposed to any approach to Thai or Fr
                    with view repatriation through Thai or Indochina.</p>
                <p>Rptd info Amembassy Rangoon 365, Amembassy London 2115, Amembassy Taipei 343,
                    Amembassy, Bangkok 888.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
